# A woodcutter's building site whose flag lands on a road is placed, and its flag splits the road into two roads that meet
# at it; a carrier works each half.
# Run it on the game view with seed 1234567812345678 and size 1:
#   sh tools/play-run.sh hut-on-road --game-view --seed 1234567812345678 --size 1 --fps 10
# On that map the castle stands at 21,4, so its flag is at 22,5. A flag goes on 28,7 (the territory ends near column 28) and a
# road of seven steps joins the two flags: five east along row 5, then down to 28,6 and 28,7. The woodcutter goes to 26,4, so
# its flag lands on the road node 27,5.
expect seed = 1234567812345678
expect size = 1
wait 0.3
click-tile 21 4
wait 0.3
button Flag
click-tile 28 7
button Flag
wait 0.3
button Road
click-tile 22 5
click-tile 23 5
click-tile 24 5
click-tile 25 5
click-tile 26 5
click-tile 27 5
click-tile 28 6
click-tile 28 7
button Road
wait 0.3
fast-forward carrier state 0x42 max 20000
wait 0.3
expect-count carrier = 1
shot one-road 26 5 5 4

button Woodcutter
click-tile 26 4
button Woodcutter
wait 0.3
expect-at 26 4 building
expect-at 27 5 flag
expect-count flag = 3
name flag 27 5 flag
expect-event flag place-flag cause placed
expect-event flag split-roads cause placed
shot split 26 5 5 4
list split

# Each half of the road holds a carrier (the site has no woodcutter to walk out: the construction, M4, sends the builder).
fast-forward until count carrier = 2 max 20000
wait 0.3
expect-count carrier = 2
shot two-carriers 26 5 5 4
list two-carriers
dump after
